# Probe limitations and corrections

- Initial offline file-URI probe attempted CSSStyleSheet.cssRules and Chromium rejected this introspection with `SecurityError: Failed to read the 'cssRules' property from 'CSSStyleSheet': Cannot access rules`. The file-origin limitation does not mean CSS failed to apply. Corrected probe records stylesheet URLs and computed background color instead; the color is rgb(13, 17, 23), matching the supplied stylesheet.
- WebKit with offline=True failed navigation to file:///C:/projects/NEPL3-doc-canonical-math-html/.tmp/html-expanded-first/docs/spec/17-math-html.html with `Page.goto: WebKit encountered an internal error`. It also failed synthetic HTTPS route fulfillment with offline=True. These attempted modes are not passes. The successful WebKit artifact-only check disables that emulated offline mode and fulfills local HTML/CSS bytes through Playwright routing without starting a server or making external requests. Chromium and Firefox successfully used real file URIs and offline=True.
- First local HTML probe mistakenly tried the Markdown-only legacy aliases in HTML. The HTML page exposes its seven encoded stable Section IDs instead. The negative legacy-alias observations remain in expanded-first/results.json. Correct stable-ID navigation is independently recorded in navigation-offline.json. No HTML legacy-alias preservation is claimed.
- First live GitHub fragment measurement waited 300 ms, which captured ongoing smooth scroll at distant targets. The initial JSON is retained as live-github-initial-scroll.json; the final measurement waits 1500 ms. Both runs found all fifteen anchors unique.
